{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_026: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical open question is whether adding image information provides any benefit over RNA alone, since this is the core hypothesis of the multimodal study and the answer determines whether ~60% of the configuration space is worth pursuing. Config_006 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) is the minimal extension of config_026: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile), adding only a pretrained image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) and the simplest fusion (concat). This isolates the effect of the image modality as cleanly as possible. If it substantially outperforms 48.5%, we know image is valuable and can invest further in image-encoder and fusion choices; if it does not, we can focus budget on RNA-side improvements (multiprofile, better RNA encoders) without wasting experiments on multimodal variants."
}

